+1. **Standing rules, chat and reading:** Batch reads, let scripts read the raw data, and keep chat to one sentence. [S7, S88]
+2. **Standing rules, merge gate:** Site files go through a worktree and the merge gate, and land with `finish-task`. [S30, S31]
+3. **Standing rules, commits:** Commit after every working step, with attribution, and leave no loose files. [S79, S105]
+4. **Standing rules, full cycle:** Run worktree, diff review and merge often. [S80]
+5. **Standing rules, owner items:** Anything that needs the owner goes on a `Note:` card on the AI board, plus one line in `findings.md`. [S32]
+6. **Standing rules, links:** Link everything you create from the site, per CLAUDE.md "Everything is linked". [S65]
+7. **Template label:** Every page shows a small label of the template or layout it uses and where it lives. Keep a short list of templates in the docs. [S78]
+8. **Sessions count:** Work out how "4,000 sessions" is computed. Counts and filters come from the session index, never from a client that loads every session. [S45, S46]
+9. **Running flash:** Find why cards flash "running" when they are not. Make state true, derived from the registry and ledger by code. [S47, S48]
+10. **Module `ai/` folders, check:** Report whether anything documents the `<module>/ai/` folders. A quick grep found nothing in `Servex/doc`, the AI docs, or the Dictate or Session readmes. [S148]
+11. **Module `ai/` folders, what they hold:** Each `<module>/ai/` folder (e.g. `ext/Session/ai`, `ux/Dictate/ai`, `ui/avatar/ai`) holds a log of events about that module, per-page voice-session transcripts (`v-<id>` plus `.summary.json`), and dated sub-folders. [S144, S145]
+12. **Module `ai/` folders, document:** Nobody remembers what these automate or where they are documented. Document in `framework/ai` what writes them, when, why, how to read them, and whether to commit them. [S146]
+13. **Module `ai/` folders, link:** Link that doc from the AI System page. [S147]
+14. **Session class, SDK check first:** Check whether the Claude Agent SDK already accounts in real time (result messages, per-message usage). If it does, lean on it; otherwise use our own script. [S10, S11]
+15. **Session class, build:** Build a `Session` class that gives the exact cost of each session, cached. Build on the token-accounting findings and plan, and don't redo that investigation. [S1, S2, S3, S4, S5]
+16. **Session class, budget:** $6, Sonnet 5.5, medium effort. [S6]
+17. **Session class, scope:** Account for every message and tool call in every session. Claude and OpenRouter stay apart, shown as "Claude $total" and "$total". [S8, S9]
+18. **Session class, runs everywhere:** One class, native ESM, usable on the server and the client, no build. [S12]
+19. **Session class, input:** Given a session id or file, `Session` loads the whole raw file in code, never in an LLM. It computes costs: tools used, time running, cache read and write, per model. Subagents roll up into the parent. [S13]
+20. **Session class, no resumes:** Never trigger an SDK resume to read cost; read files only. [S38]
+21. **Session class, cache:** Never reprocess a huge raw file on load. Process it once into a per-session `session.jsonl`, and let the page load only that small cache. [S15, S16, S18]
+22. **Session class, incremental:** After the first pass, read only new lines and skip message ids already counted. [S17]
+23. **Session class, streaming:** Reuse the stream from `2026-10-08/live-not-polling` (read its `findings.md`); build no second stream. [S22, S23]
+24. **Session class, display:** Two modes of the same class: a preview row for the grid and a click-through detail view. [S14]
+25. **Session class, speed:** Measure the bytes and requests the Sessions page loads, before and after, and report both, because the site is already slow on mobile. [S19]
+26. **Per-session folder:** `ai/sessions/<slug>/` holds `session.jsonl` (usage, costs) beside `page.jsonl` (page data). [S20]
+27. **Session class, deliverable `findings.md`:** It says whether the SDK accounts in real time (with evidence) and which source is the truth per provider. [S24, S25]
+28. **Session class, deliverable `Session.js`:** Put it in the right module folder, for server and client, with a node test. The test loads a real session file and checks the total against `Server/session-cost.mjs` and the reconcile result. Report the gap; target 0. [S26]
+29. **Session class, deliverable script:** `Server/session-summary.mjs <session-id|file>` prints the same summary, so agents ask a script rather than read a file. [S28]
+30. **Session class, deliverable doc:** A `sessions/doc/` note on the shape of `session.jsonl`, loading, saving and timing, linked from the readme. [S29]
+31. **Sessions storage, inventory first:** Find and document every pattern where sessions live, as a table in `sessions/doc/` (pattern, example path, count, how it is read). [S72]
+32. **Sessions storage, three stores today:** Answer in `findings.md` first, then fix. Session cards link to two places: the date tree `framework/ai/2026/10/07/session-<short-uuid>/` (opens the Inbox view, little info) and `framework/ai/sessions/mastermind-servex-10` (opens as a right column, which is nice). Today there are three stores: UUID folders (the cache), named folders under `ai/sessions/`, and date-tree `session-<id>` folders where the VS Code tabs live. [S40, S41, S42]
+33. **Sessions storage, one store:** Pick the date tree, the owner's preference. Convert with a non-destructive script: move and rename, no rewrite, old links resolve through a resolver. [S43]
+34. **Sessions storage, alternative:** Name the alternative store in `findings.md`. [S44]
+35. **Sessions storage, location:** The later addendum puts raw data under `ai/sessions/YYYY/MM/DD/`. Today many sessions sit directly in `framework/ai/` (46 hyphen-dated dirs plus `ai/2026/MM/DD/`), and children go inside the parent's directory. [S70, S71]
+36. **Sessions storage, merge by script:** Dry-run, `git mv`, a manifest of old to new paths, old paths still resolve. No AI rewriting. Every session renders the same detail view. [S73]
+37. **Sessions storage, addendum:** One store, real names, a compact grid. [S39]
+38. **Session names:** Many cards are named "monorepo", the repo name. Derive a useful name instead: the task or card title, the first real prompt, or the agent id. [S49, S50]
+39. **Session names, going forward:** Every session and task gets a proper name. [S51]
+40. **Session nesting by path:** Child sessions nest as real subdirectories (`parent/child`, `parent/child/grandchild`), not a `--` suffix. [S52]
+41. **Tags and alerts, model:** Sessions carry **tags** (a reference to a class, page, system or file) and **alerts** (needs attention, with a priority). [S33, S34]
+42. **Tags and alerts, writing:** Agents never hand-write JSONL. A log tool stamps time and author. Any minion can call it for any session, outside the session's own prompt, to append tags and alerts to `session.jsonl`. [S21, S35]
+43. **Tags and alerts, first writer:** The task-audit mastermind (`2026-10-08/task-audit`) writes first. Agree the line shapes with its `requirements.md` addendum. This work owns the tool and the table. [S37]
+44. **Sessions table, filter and sort by tag:** Add a prioritized "needs attention" filter. [S36]
+45. **Sessions grid, status bars:** Replace the big 5-hour and weekly tiles with the progress bars and pace marker the Dashboard already has. Reuse that component, one of everything. [S54, S55]
+46. **Sessions grid, compact:** Cut the wasted space above the grid, and make the list as compact as possible. [S56, S57]
+47. **Sessions grid, quick filter:** Add an "in flight / now / active" filter beside the existing checkboxes. [S58]
+48. **Sessions grid, sort:** Add sort toggles (recency, cost, model) to flip between chronological and cost views. [S59]
+49. **Sessions grid, state column:** Move the state icon to the first column, as important as the name. [S60]
+50. **Sessions grid, child rows:** Show child rows under their parent, collapsed by default, with the rolled-up cost. [S53]
+51. **Sessions grid, sub-pages:** Host sub-pages inside the Sessions tab, since the grid fills it. [S63]
+52. **Sessions system, readme and decisions:** Write a readme and a decisions doc for the Sessions system. List the owner's asks and decisions priority-ordered with the top first, linked from the tab. [S64]
+53. **Sessions grid, scope:** Don't over-build yet. [S61]
+54. **Master-detail, one mode:** One open mode and one location, a master-detail layout. The IN FLIGHT strip stays top priority. [S66, S67]
+55. **Master-detail, right column:** Every card opens in the right-hand column, as `mastermind-servex-10` does. Stop the `ai/2026/10/07/session-<id>` links that jump to the Inbox view. [S68]
+56. **Master-detail, one route:** One route per session whatever its storage, and the same detail view however you arrive. [S62, S69]
+57. **Master-detail, reuse:** The grid is the responsive navigator for the detail pane, like the Inbox list. Reuse the existing master-detail/columns mechanism. [S74, S77]
+58. **Master-detail, wide screens:** A default 50/50 split, resizable. The detail fills its side with no fixed width (it stops short after resizing today). [S75]
+59. **Master-detail, narrow screens:** The 7-column table becomes compact inbox-style cards with wrapped fields, not tall. Clicking another session swaps the detail. [S76]
+60. **Sessions grid, check:** The preview row and detail view, both backed by `Session`, pass at four widths, then merge. [S27]
+61. **Inbox, document:** Document where cards are saved, how they are created (MCP tool or manual), and how the dashboard, Sessions tab and log read them. [S131]
+62. **Inbox, session context:** Wrap inbox cards in a session context card (session icon and name). The owner then sees which top-level sessions run, can drill in, and sees cost. [S132]
+63. **AI system docs, role:** A system mastermind, a fresh Sonnet 5.5 pointed at a directory, not a resumed session. Read `CLAUDE.md`, then the readme chain down to `ai/` and `Servex/`. [S84, S85]
+64. **AI system docs, budget:** $5 total. Run `node Server/usage-now.mjs` before each spawn. Minions are Haiku 5.5, Sonnet only for UI and OO code. [S86]
+65. **AI system docs, docs first:** Additive edits and proposals only. No API changes, no moves, nothing destructive. [S87]
+66. **AI system docs, brief:** Show the structure of the AI system as classes. [S81, S82]
+67. **AI system docs, reuse:** Find the existing class-doc mechanism (`ext/Doc`, the class-rendering template). Extend it; don't build a second. [S95]
+68. **AI system docs, class cards:** Where a thing is a class, show a card: icon, name, core API, and the most important properties and methods picked by judgement, no weighting. Add live instances where they exist, such as Servex's `Pool`, `Usage`, `Agents`, `Dispatcher` and `Heartbeat`. [S93, S94]
+69. **AI system docs, Servex card:** A class card focused on the AI system (tools/MCP, agents, sessions, spawning, pool, usage, dispatcher), not its self-monitoring, restart or server-list side. [S128]
+70. **AI system docs, at a glance:** Make these clear: Servex, the Agent SDK, OpenRouter and local models, sessions, models (`/framework/ai/models`), the dashboard, the inbox and tasks. [S96]
+71. **AI system docs, SDK section:** Explain how Servex spawns agents through `query()`, how tools reach it via in-process MCP, how session files are written, and `sdk-ts` vs `claude-vscode` entrypoints. [S97]
+72. **AI system docs, stale pages:** Some linked pages look stale (e.g. `AI/minions`). The mastermind-vs-minion line is not a hard boundary. [S91, S92]
+73. **AI system docs, architecture view:** The `framework/ai` System tab becomes a class architecture view: which classes exist and how they fit. [S127]
+74. **AI system docs, `ai/` and `Servex/` readmes:** Write `readme.md` and `architecture.md` for `ai/` and `Servex/`, each linking the others. Reuse the agents' reports (`docs-vs-code-audit`, `task-audit`, `token-accounting`) rather than redoing them. [S102, S104]
+75. **AI system docs, history:** `ai/doc/meta/history.md`, main events only, one line each: problem, solution, deep link to the session or task. Copy no content. [S130]
+76. **AI system docs, findings:** `findings.md` lists what changed, what is stale or missing, and which AI pieces are not yet classes and should be (a short list, no refactor now). It also carries any Note for the owner. [S103]
